 (2, "Ancient writers do not quote or mention it.", ["F22"]),

 (3, "The treatise is a compendium of literary exemplars, with about fifty authors across a thousand years mentioned or quoted, Homer, Demosthenes and the Greek dramatists among them, and it quotes a passage of Genesis, which is unusual for its century.", ["F12", "F45", "F13"]),
 (3, "Its sublime acts on the audience by transport: \"The effect of elevated language upon an audience is not persuasion but transport\", and it leads listeners \"not to persuasion, but to ecstasy\".", ["F27", "F17"]),
