 (5, "In its tenth chapter the treatise names as a cause of sublimity the choice of the most fitting elements and their combination into one body, and gives Sappho as its example: she takes the symptoms that attend erotic madness from what accompanies them and from truth itself (10.1).", ["F57", "F58"]),
